{"pages":[{"kind":"narration","speaker":"","text":"Summon-light drops Renna Holt, Mirelle Voss, and Edren Marr into a cramped stone ruin. Armed goblins rush through the broken stone with their weapons raised."},{"kind":"dialogue","speaker":"Edren Marr","text":"Goblins—I can’t fight them!"},{"kind":"narration","speaker":"","text":"Edren bolts with his hooked pole clutched across his chest. A goblin cuts him down from behind; he hits the debris and does not rise.

[ HERO LOST: Edren Marr, one-star ]"},{"kind":"narration","speaker":"","text":"Mirelle steps beside Edren's body and drives her red-tasseled spear into the foremost goblin, holding its shaft across the narrow ruin. Renna slips behind her shoulder, wall at her back, and sends an arrow into a goblin trying to press around the spear. It falls among the stones."},{"kind":"narration","speaker":"","text":"A goblin comes along the broken wall toward Renna. She ducks beneath its blade, cuts inward, and looses an arrow into its ribs before returning toward Mirelle's spear.

The others hook the spear aside long enough to slash Mirelle's upper arm. Blood marks her sleeve. She surges into the press, breaks one goblin's weapon arm aside with the spear's butt, and drives the leaf-blade into its chest. One armed goblin remains before her."}]}

{"pages":[{"kind":"narration","speaker":"","text":"Five columns of premium summon-light descend into Niflheim’s lobby and resolve into five newly summoned Heroes around the circle.

[ 20-Gem pack purchase accepted ]
[ Premium Summons performed: 5 ]"},{"kind":"narration","speaker":"","text":"Iselle zips into the center of the fading summon-light, wings buzzing, her smile bright and sharp."},{"kind":"dialogue","speaker":"Iselle","text":"Welcome to Niflheim, fresh arrivals—the lobby! That silent Master owns this roster and decides who gets deployed. The gate leads to a separate, lethal floor. Once deployed, you choose how you fight; clear the objective and survivors return. The ordinary gate will not bring you back early. Death or synthesis is permanent. Cheerful, simple, and absolutely final!"}]}
